  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#606b43b065bdd51ca079884c69ea1c43919187ea769a33845e7cce1ae1125624</id>
    <title>Useful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-19T00:35:59Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-1" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">When a neighbour is new, offering a specific welcome—such as pointing out the nearest bus stop—makes it easier to accept help than a vague “let me know”.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#93591821810b7432a3853edb71803e1b0083caeee6f7feca7ef973474c5fe2b7</id>
    <title>Hopeful</title>
    <updated>2026-11-19T00:35:59Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-2" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Bumblebees can learn to pull a string to reach a food reward, and can learn the task by watching another bee—a striking example of social learning in insects.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://positivitybriefing.com/feed.atom#4aea8996723b943e3139c01063bb07a7d0ed383e916e46c8a9cbb6cc67ca428b</id>
    <title>Action</title>
    <updated>2026-11-19T00:35:59Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://positivitybriefing.com/#item-3" type="text/html"/>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In under five minutes, check your front door or shared entrance for a trip hazard, then move one loose shoe, bag or parcel safely out of the way.</div>
    </content>
  </entry>
